        {
          "id": 1869403095,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "get_fake_header_value() call returns dynamic memory, but that is in the pinfo->pool scope and thus is freed automatically. So there is no real memory leak thanks to the automatic garbage collection, simply Coverity is not aware of this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
